  "2026-07-12T08:31:29.065Z",codex-root,"Implementation start: live frontier confirms sdk/runtime.ts has 12 effective lines of headroom; this active item owns a behavior-preserving per-domain dispatch split bundled with pm-3mna and pm-zwpp."
  "2026-07-12T09:50:05.795Z",codex-root,"Evidence: annotation extraction removed one CLI-private domain module and 13 private-core baseline imports while keeping the static boundary gate green. The broader sdk/runtime.ts per-domain dispatch decomposition remains open and is not claimed complete."
  "2026-07-12T11:57:15.410Z",maintainer-agent,"Census delta 2026-07-12: src/cli/main.ts 3369->3376/3400 (+7 effective, canonical normalizeLine method) — reset-on-entry seam for runtime-extension snapshot caches (pm-8fxc fix inside runPmCli). sdk/runtime.ts steady 3388/3400 after PR#524 (annotation kernel landed as NEW src/sdk/annotations.ts — precedent that new SDK domains can bypass the runtime.ts cap; see pm-usfg frontier note). Decomposition seam priorities unchanged."
  "2026-07-24T12:05:45.376Z",claude-code-agent,"Current effective-LOC census using the static gate normalization: src/core/extensions/loader.ts is exactly 3400/3400; src/cli/register-mutation.ts 3398; src/cli/main.ts 3389; src/sdk/extension.ts 3362; sdk/governance/validate.ts 3263; sdk/runtime.ts 3231; sdk/query/search.ts 3053. The gate still passes, but loader has zero headroom and three additional infrastructure modules are above 99% of the ceiling. This item remains the canonical behavior-preserving decomposition owner; thresholds must not be raised."
  "2026-08-04T09:18:07.013Z","harness:codex","Fresh repository census 2026-08-04: 51 src TypeScript files exceed 1,000 raw lines. Largest units are src/sdk/runtime.ts 3,963; sdk/extension.ts 3,801; sdk/governance/validate.ts 3,740; core/extensions/loader.ts 3,653; cli/register-mutation.ts 3,558; sdk/query/search.ts 3,412; lifecycle/update.ts 3,153; lifecycle/create.ts 3,148; and cli/main.ts 3,137. Static quality still passes because effective-LOC ceilings are not the same as raw maintainability size. Preserve behavior and public exports while decomposing; do not raise caps."
  "2026-09-19T16:30:01.616Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: original files fully inspected before extraction. Public compatibility exports and test hooks retained; no cap or coverage threshold raised. Search and CLI focused baseline 272 tests passed before and after extraction. Infrastructure now additionally separates native SDK action dispatch/schema, manifest parsing/registration validation, and all three completion renderers. Full quality and coverage validation in progress."
  "2026-09-19T16:44:19.793Z","harness:codex","Validation caught stale replication inventory paths after mechanical extraction. Repointed contracts to completion/zsh and runtime/actions, preserving all member assertions and refusal counts (7 = 3 + 3 + 1). Existing receipt docs/tests remain unchanged with item-scoped expiring relocation dispositions; no gate thresholds relaxed. Lowered ESLint suppression ceiling 109 to 108."
  "2026-09-19T16:48:44.314Z","harness:codex","Candidate packed artifact passed 11-step installed agent sessions under both npm/Node and Bun, including public SDK complete-list reads. Published 2026.9.19 separately passed the same installed checks. Pre-push GitHub inventory: no pre-existing open PR, zero open Dependabot/code-scanning/secret-scanning alerts; issue #1246 already links canonical pm-z3ez. Current Sentry required reliability gate passes with no blocking recent issues; fresh backend telemetry events observed. Coverage owns the build-consumer lease, so linked-test execution is serialized after coverage to avoid lock-wait timeouts."
  "2026-09-19T16:51:11.178Z","harness:codex","Mechanical review evidence: TypeScript AST body comparison against the branch base found 115 unchanged CLI functions, 126 SDK runtime functions, 68 loader functions and 22 completion functions. Only generateFishScript changed to extract its existing multiline tag resolver. Search comparison found 80 unchanged functions; three body changes inline their corresponding three removed single-use wrappers. Complete golden outputs remain byte-identical."
  "2026-09-19T17:01:13.604Z","harness:codex","Linked seven-file infrastructure regression suite passed. Four-project TypeScript checks, 100 percent module/export/member documentation gates, zero-clone profiles, SDK export snapshot (zero classified changes), compatibility contracts and token budgets pass. SDK import cost and CLI transport performance gates pass when measured without concurrent coverage. Graph composition and record integrity pass after linking the three compatibility-upgrade peers mentioned in the inventory. Full coverage rerun follows synchronized script and provider suppression limits of 108."
  "2026-09-19T17:02:01.622Z","harness:codex","Correction to the preceding validation note: record integrity passed, but the graph-composition result still rejected three newly added generic related edges. Reclassified those dependency-intake edges as discovered_from, reflecting the actual live major-upgrade triage that selected the compatible scanner update. No graph bound was raised. Awaiting the full graph verdict before claiming it passes."
  "2026-09-19T17:10:28.763Z","harness:codex","Final coverage: 9057 tests in 717 files; exact 100/100/100/100 with zero uncovered counts (64759 statements, 49447 branches, 13457 functions, 61969 lines). Effective source sizes: main 1981, loader 2548, SDK runtime 2447, mutation registration 2450, completion 44; every target is below 2720. Public SDK snapshot has zero classified changes. Linked tests, manual/installed/package acceptance and byte-identical golden outputs pass. A final serialized quality run is settling before push; hosted review/merge evidence is not yet claimed."
notes[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-12T08:20:08.773Z",maintainer-agent,"2026-07-12 census refresh (same method: static-quality-gate normalizeLine over src/**/*.ts, cap 3400). Delta vs the 07-11 body census:\n- sdk/runtime.ts 3236 -> 3388 (99.6% of cap, 12 effective lines of headroom) — now the #1 at-risk file, overtaking main.ts (3369, unchanged). Growth is the SDK-first slices themselves: PR#512 (plan), PR#517 (ranked atomic selection), PR#520 (schema boundaries) all land action surface here.\n- SEQUENCING CONSEQUENCE: pm-3mna S1 (next SDK slice, current recommended frontier) cannot merge without blowing the gate. The runtime.ts seam owned here (per-domain action tables + shared dispatch kernel, runAction semantics-oracle preserved) must land FIRST — either as a standalone prep PR or as 3mna S1's first commit. Coordination note posted on pm-usfg.\n- context.ts crossed 2000 (2011) — watch, not owned here (context belongs to pm-oslr slice relief first).\n- create.ts 2851->2789, update.ts 2758->2697 (PR#523 relief); register-mutation 3037, completion 2818 (+5/+9 noise); search.ts/loader.ts/extension.ts/validate.ts unchanged.\n- Files >=3000: 7; >=2000: 17. Priority bumped 2->1 on the strength of the runtime.ts headroom."
  "2026-07-12T08:43:58.354Z",codex-root,"Execution rule from user escalation (23rd recurrence): this active delivery lane must not stop at partial implementation, local verification, commit, PR creation, pending checks, or pending bot review. Continue through the requested green reviewed PR, merge, merged-head/release/Sentry/telemetry proof, tracker closure, claim release, and return to main; only a genuine exhausted blocker permits stopping."
  "2026-07-12T19:14:59.833Z",maintainer-agent,"2026-07-12 directive recurrence (too-many/too-long, document-only): the folder-density half is now owned by sibling pm-kb5h (source-tree directory fan-out, 6-tranche blueprint). Fence: yh8r = intra-file effective-LOC decomposition of near-cap files; kb5h = inter-file directory regrouping. Any physical move of a yh8r target file happens WITH its yh8r split (or its usfg slice), never as a standalone kb5h move — one migration per file. LOC census unchanged from this morning's note (runtime.ts 3388 = #1 at-risk)."
  "2026-07-13T09:49:54.816Z",maintainer-agent,"Census refresh 2026-07-13 (review pass #78, gate-normalized LOC vs 3400 cap): main.ts 3386 (99.6% — 14 lines of headroom, next commander registration will likely breach), sdk/runtime.ts 3367 (99.0%), core/extensions/loader.ts 3312 (97.4%), commands/extension.ts 3239 (95.3%), register-mutation.ts 3066 (90.2%), commands/validate.ts 3052 (89.8%). main.ts is now the most urgent seam (was runtime.ts at pass #71). Raw wc -l overcounts (~300 lines/file) — always measure via normalizeLine from scripts/release/static-quality-gate.mjs."
  "2026-07-13T14:24:31.363Z",maintainer-agent,"LOC census refresh 2026-07-13 (post PR#543, gate-normalized vs 3400 cap): src/cli/main.ts 3386 (headroom 14, unchanged — still the most urgent seam); src/sdk/runtime.ts 3365 (headroom 35 — grew again via PR#543 import rerouting and is now the second-tightest seam; each SDK promotion slice adds imports/exports here, so the pm-usfg slices 3mna/oxrw/4a7m/oslr will keep pressing it — runtime.ts partition should precede or accompany the next slice); src/cli/commands/search.ts 3359 (headroom 41, unchanged). No gate violations; never raise the cap."
  "2026-07-15T19:11:25.602Z",maintainer-agent,"LOC census refresh 2026-07-15 (review pass #89, post PR#568, gate-normalized vs 3400 cap): src/sdk/runtime.ts 3400 — HEADROOM ZERO, the gate is saturated; the next non-comment line added anywhere in the file fails quality:static. main.ts 3377 (headroom 23), search.ts 3359 (41, unchanged), sdk/extension.ts 3349 (51), extensions/loader.ts 3312 (88, unchanged), governance/validate.ts 3103, register-mutation.ts 3074. Consequence for sequencing: the runtime.ts partition can no longer \"precede or accompany\" the next pm-usfg slice — it must land FIRST, since pm-oslr (execution/diagnostics) and pm-ju83 (relationship registry, current pm-next recommended) both add runtime.ts exports/imports. No gate violations today; never raise the cap."
  "2026-07-17T10:22:32.438Z",maintainer-agent,"LOC census refresh 2026-07-17 (review pass #96, post PR#577, gate-normalized vs 3400 cap): src/sdk/runtime.ts 3398 (headroom 2 — PR#577's graph-context exports re-pressed the seam that the PR#571-lane net -7 had bought; effectively saturated again, any two non-comment lines added fail quality:static). main.ts 3384 (headroom 16), sdk/query/search.ts 3371 (29), sdk/extension.ts 3349 (51), extensions/loader.ts 3312 (88), governance/validate.ts 3103, register-mutation.ts 3088. Sequencing signal: pm-ju83 (pm next's recommended, last pm-ds3b blocker) is an SDK-export-adding slice — it cannot land without either the runtime.ts partition shipping first/with it or routing its exports through a new subpath module (PR#571-lane sdk/test+sdk/diagnostics folder precedent). Cross-noted on pm-ju83."
  "2026-07-17T21:43:58.946Z",maintainer-agent,"LOC frontier RESHUFFLED by PR#580 (2026-07-17 gate-metric measurement, non-comment non-blank lines vs 3400 cap): runtime.ts dropped 3398 -> 3036 (runtime-input.ts extraction, ~364 headroom — the headroom-2 saturation is RESOLVED). New near-saturation order: cli/main.ts 3385 (headroom 15, NEW frontier holder), sdk/query/search.ts 3371 (29), sdk/extension.ts 3349 (51), core/extensions/loader.ts 3312 (88), sdk/governance/validate.ts 3103, cli/register-mutation.ts 3088. Any feature touching main.ts or search.ts now risks tripping the gate first — decomposition priority should follow this order. Never raise the 3400 cap."
  "2026-07-19T04:07:31.735Z",maintainer-agent,"Effective-LOC census 2026-07-19 (gate counting rules, cap 3400): main.ts 3400 (100.0% - AT the cap, the next effective line added fails CI static gates), query/search.ts 3371 (99.1%), extensions/loader.ts 3367 (99.0%), sdk/extension.ts 3349 (98.5%). Deltas since the 2026-07-11 body census: main +31, search +41, loader +55, extension +110. The four top files now have a combined headroom of 113 lines. Decomposition of main.ts is effectively a prerequisite for any feature that wires a new command (every wiring site includes main.ts)."
  "2026-09-19T16:46:03.150Z","harness:codex","September architecture decision: retain mutable CLI invocation state, activation rollback, module cache/import.meta.url anchoring, and SDK dispatch lifecycle in their original owners. Extract pure argv/selection/telemetry classification, manifest and registration contracts, native SDK handlers/schema adapters, and shell-specific completion renderers. Nine complete shell outputs (three shells, three configurations) matched the original byte for byte. register-mutation is already below the 2720 effective-line target from prior delivery and needs no redundant decomposition."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-19T16:46:03.853Z","harness:codex","A behavior-preserving module move must update ownership inventories as well as imports: refusal counts should be conserved across new modules; replication declarations must follow the implementation. When removing a complexity suppression, lower its enforced budget in the same change."
  "2026-09-19T17:03:06.017Z","harness:codex","Suppression ratchets have two authoritative declarations: MAX_ESLINT_SUPPRESSIONS in the static gate and repository-quality provider_args in gate-registry.json. Run the release-automation suppression contract before a full coverage pass after reducing the baseline. Performance budgets should run without concurrent full coverage to avoid CPU-contention false negatives."
